# Managed by .dotfiles — edit this file, not `crontab -e`.
# Everything between the BEGIN/END markers is replaced on each ./install run.
# Any cron jobs you add outside these markers are preserved.
#
# The daily `mackup backup -f` that used to live here is gone. Two reasons:
#
#  1. It ran on every machine, making both Macs mackup writers. mackup has no
#     conflict resolution, so the older config silently destroys the newer one.
#     The backup now lives in the MacBook's host profile only.
#
#  2. It failed silently for about three years. cron on modern macOS has no
#     Full Disk Access, so every ~/Library path was denied, and cron's output
#     went nowhere. Backups stopped around March 2023 and nothing surfaced it
#     until a second Mac was set up in September 2026.
#
# Replaced by the launchd agent misc/dk.graunephar.mackup-backup.plist, which
# logs to ~/Library/Logs/mackup-backup.log and verifies its own writes.
#
# BEGIN dotfiles-managed
# END dotfiles-managed
